# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The leaf menu offers the applications that are installed, and choosing
# one STARTS it: the editor opens a window of its own over the session,
# which is the same route any application takes.
wait 12
click 980 20
wait 4
note document applications have their own category and icons
menu-pick Documents
wait 4
expect-menu Editor|TikuReader
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-app-menu.png
note the editor and reader retain their app icons and launch identities
note choosing the editor starts it; its window arrives over the session
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
key Escape
wait 20
expect-no-title Edit
note and an editor with TYPING in it does not die by the same key: the
note kit's own alert asks first, inside the application's window -- no
note shell involved, which is the point of the alert being the kit's
click 980 20
wait 4
menu-pick Documents
wait 4
menu-pick Editor
wait 90
expect-title Edit
key x
wait 4
key Escape
wait 8
expect-title Edit
note Escape in the question presses Cancel, the safe road: still standing
key Escape
wait 6
expect-title Edit
note asked again, Return safely cancels rather than discarding typing
key Escape
wait 6
key Return
wait 8
expect-title Edit
key Escape
wait 6
note Discard now requires an explicit click in the unsaved-work question
shot /tmp/tiku-editor-question.png
click 592 318
wait 20
expect-no-title Edit
